From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 09:32:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libprocessgroup: give recovery a cgroup-v1-only profile too

Recovery has its own descriptor file, cgroups.recovery.json, which I missed
when converting cgroups.json to a v1-only layout. It declared nothing but the
cgroup v2 root, so on this 3.10 kernel recovery could not boot at all:

  libprocessgroup: Failed to make and chown /sys/fs/cgroup/uid_0: No such file
  init: cpuset cgroup controller is not mounted!
  init: Could not restart process 'ueventd': createProcessGroup(0, 330) failed
  init: critical process 'ueventd' exited 4 times before boot completed
  init: InitFatalReboot: signal 6

The path in that error is the giveaway: '/sys/fs/cgroup/uid_0' is the v2 root,
whereas the ROM (running the patched cgroups.json) fails as '/uid_0' with an
empty base. Two different files, two different failures.

Dropped the v2 root and declared cpuset as an Optional v1 controller, which
also addresses init's 'cpuset cgroup controller is not mounted' complaint.
With no v2 hierarchy the path is empty and createProcessGroupInternal's guard
returns success, so ueventd starts.

Worth noting the diagnostic value: recovery is a far smaller environment than
the ROM and boots in seconds, so it is a much faster loop for shaking out
early-init problems.
---
 libprocessgroup/profiles/cgroups.recovery.json | 16 ++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libprocessgroup/profiles/cgroups.recovery.json b/libprocessgroup/profiles/cgroups.recovery.json
index e27525262..16fd55269 100644
--- a/libprocessgroup/profiles/cgroups.recovery.json
+++ b/libprocessgroup/profiles/cgroups.recovery.json
@@ -1,8 +1,12 @@
 {
-  "Cgroups2": {
-    "Path": "/sys/fs/cgroup",
-    "Mode": "0755",
-    "UID": "root",
-    "GID": "root"
-  }
+  "Cgroups": [
+    {
+      "Controller": "cpuset",
+      "Path": "/dev/cpuset",
+      "Mode": "0755",
+      "UID": "root",
+      "GID": "root",
+      "Optional": true
+    }
+  ]
 }
